		)
		(uuid "bd3b0f6a-b430-4144-a920-850236a98ffe")
	)
	(text "How it works\n1. U1 (NE555) oscillates at f = 1.44/((R1+2*R4)*C11) = 75 kHz, ~53 % duty.\n2. IC1 (IR2302) drives the Q1/Q2 half-bridge (built-in dead time, D2/C3 bootstrap).\n3. The square wave at SW drives the series-resonant tank C5 + TX coil (J2).\n4. RX coil (J3) + C7 resonate at the same 75 kHz; D3/D4 double the voltage into C6.\n5. IC2 (LM7805) regulates to 5 V (J4). D5 protects IC2, D1 clamps over-voltage.\nCoils: L = 1/((2*pi*75 kHz)^2 * 0.1 uF) = 45 uH each (~15 turns, 60 mm dia).\nTX GND and GND_RX are NOT connected: energy crosses only via the magnetic field.\nC5/C7: polypropylene film >= 250 V (>100 V at resonance). VRAW must stay above ~7.5 V for the 7805."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 213.36 195.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "edc0fed6-7f45-41db-84ca-e04b85267d81")
	)
